<title>FRANCE: Estimated breakdown of French EU grain bids.</title>
<headline>Estimated breakdown of French EU grain bids.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Traders gave the following estimated breakdown of bids placed through France for European Union grain at a weekly tender on Thursday.</p>
<p>SOFT WHEAT</p>
<p>    Cumulative volume     Refund</p>
<p>    (tonnes)		  (Ecus/tonne)</p>
<p>    173,000		   18.00 or less</p>
<p>    280,000		   18.50 or less</p>
<p>    393,700		   19.00 or less</p>
<p>    550,700		   22.35 or less</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Cumulative volume     Refund</p>
<p>    (tonnes)		  (Ecus/tonne)</p>
<p>	3,000		   31.00</p>
<p>     65,000		   31.90 or less</p>
<p>    132,000		   32.95 or less</p>
<p>    182,000		   33.49 or less</p>
<p>An official at French cereals office ONIC earlier reported bids for 550,700 tonnes of soft wheat at refunds between 16.49 and 22.35 Ecus per tonne and for 182,000 tonnes of barley at refunds between 31.00 and 33.49 Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>The official also reported bids for 5,000 tonnes of rye at refunds between 31.49 and 31.95 Ecus per tonne.</p>
</text>
